.SH GLOBAL OPTIONS
\-\-json opts into JSON. Help and version remain text. Duplicate global options fail before help/version short circuits.
.SH SAFETY
Removal refuses dirty worktrees and unproven ownership. Dry runs acquire no locks and perform no mutations; execution rechecks state. Workspace removal preserves local branches. Repository removal deletes the containing mirror and its local refs and commits. Save needed work outside that mirror before repository cleanup; network operations require explicit authorization. Modified or foreign generated AGENTS.md requires explicit consent. Crash records require manual inspection, never automatic recovery.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 means success. 1 means an error on stderr, or a partial result on stdout. Inspect structured results before retrying.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
OUTPOST_HOME selects the state home, default ~/.outpost. OUTPOST_GIT_TIMEOUT_MS sets the Git timeout in milliseconds.
.SH OFFLINE GUIDANCE
Use outpost docs, outpost docs recovery, outpost skill show, or outpost skill path \-\-json.
